<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="theme-color" content="#0c1829"><title>TABOR UNIVERSAL NODE — Mission Control</title><style>:root{font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif;color-scheme:dark;background:#091827;color:#f4f7fa}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:radial-gradient(circle at 52% -10%,#334c78,transparent 65%),#091827}main{max-width:1120px;margin:auto;padding:20px}a{color:#f3d28f}h1{font-size:clamp(2.2rem,6vw,4.6rem);line-height:1.04;margin:14px 0}h2{margin-top:0}.sub{color:#bcd0e1;line-height:1.6}.hero,.panel{border:1px solid #627d9c;border-radius:19px;padding:20px;background:#142a42;margin-bottom:15px}.kicker{color:#edcb8f;font-size:.82rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.16em}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(240px,1fr));gap:14px}label{display:block;font-size:.91rem;margin:10px 0;color:#d1e2ee}input,select,textarea{display:block;width:100%;padding:12px;margin-top:5px;border-radius:10px;border:1px solid #81a1c0;background:#0c2237;color:white;font:inherit}textarea{min-height:100px}button{padding:12px 18px;background:#e6bb70;border:0;border-radius:11px;color:#182433;font-weight:800;font:inherit;cursor:pointer}button:focus-visible,a:focus-visible,input:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #fff}.box{background:#223b55;border:1px solid #63839b;border-radius:13px;padding:15px}.symbol{text-align:center;font-size:clamp(4rem,10vw,7rem);color:#f5d19a;line-height:1;margin:10px}.axis{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center}.center{width:28px;height:28px;background:#fff1bd;border:6px solid #edc478;border-radius:50%;position:absolute;box-shadow:0 0 20px #e7cc9c}.spin{font-size:140px;line-height:1;display:block;animation:spin 22s linear infinite;transform-origin:center}@keyframes spin{to{transform:rotate(360deg)}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.spin{animation:none}}.good{color:#a2eed3}.warn{color:#ffe0a0}.bad{color:#ffb0bd}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;background:#0a1f32;padding:15px;border-radius:12px;max-height:420px;overflow:auto}nav a{margin-right:16px}.foot{color:#bbccda;font-size:.84rem}.checks{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px}.checks>div{flex:1;min-width:170px}.headrow{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:8px}</style></head><body><main><nav><a href="../index.html">← FACTORY</a><a href="./index.html">Universal Node Visualizer</a><a href="../build-order/index.html">Build Order</a></nav><div class="hero"><div class="kicker">𓋹 TABOR INFINITUM V∞ · NATHAN AI · MISSION CONTROL</div><h1>THE ONE AT THE CENTER<br>OF THE SPINNING X</h1><div class="grid"><div class="axis"><span class="spin" aria-hidden="true">✕</span><span class="center" aria-hidden="true"></span></div><div><p class="sub"><strong>1 + 1 = 2 · 1 − 1 = 0.</strong> Expand information without erasing original identities. Revoking permission blocks future authorized work. Preserve the observer—the One—and check evidence before proposing action.</p><p class="sub">Body → Earth → Cosmos → Unknown. The spinning X is a symbolic, interactive reference frame centered on Earth. It is not an absolute stationary point in the universe.</p><button id="run">Advance rotating-X simulation</button><p id="rotation" role="status">Ready</p></div></div></div>
<div class="panel"><h2>Find a problem → build a verified response</h2><p class="sub">Choose a demonstration or describe a problem. This engine drafts a reviewable intervention plan, never controls equipment or claims to fix an unseen phenomenon.</p><div class="grid"><label>Start from an example<select id="example"><option value="">Custom issue</option><option value="0">Body · illustrative concern</option><option value="1">Earth · environmental observation</option><option value="2">Software · checksum failure</option><option value="3">Cosmos · unconfirmed telescope signal</option></select></label><label>Domain<select id="domain"><option>body</option><option>community</option><option>earth</option><option>cosmos</option><option>unknown</option><option>software</option><option>hardware</option></select></label><label>Risk<select id="risk"><option>information</option><option>routine</option><option>safety-critical</option></select></label><label>Evidence<select id="evidence"><option>observed</option><option>hypothesis</option><option>verified</option><option>simulated</option></select></label></div><label>Issue title<input id="title" maxlength="150" value="Synthetic river observation"></label><label>Description<textarea id="description" maxlength="3000">An illustrative temperature shift is shown by a simulated sensor packet, not a real environmental measurement.</textarea></label><div class="grid"><label>Severity (1–5)<input id="severity" type="number" min="1" max="5" value="2"></label><label>Source reference (optional, not itself verification)<input id="source" placeholder="Source publication or observation ID"></label></div><label><input id="consent" type="checkbox" style="display:inline;width:auto"> Appropriate consent has been confirmed for proposal review</label><label><input id="approval" type="checkbox" style="display:inline;width:auto"> A responsible owner has approved reviewing the proposal</label><p><button id="assess">Analyze and plan</button></p></div>
<div class="panel"><div class="headrow"><h2>Three Engines + Scientific Evidence</h2><strong id="mode" class="warn">Not yet assessed</strong></div><div id="gates" class="grid"></div><h3>Action and verification sequence</h3><ol id="steps"></ol><p id="advice" class="sub"></p><p class="bad">No automated real-world intervention, medical diagnosis, independent evidence verification, or hardware actuation is enabled.</p><button id="export">Export local assessment JSON</button></div>
<div class="panel"><h2>Hardware interfaces</h2><p class="sub">These are versioned contracts for future owner-authorized sensor adapters—not connections to a medical device, spacecraft, or environmental monitor.</p><label>Example sensor class<select id="device"><option value="environment-sensor">Environmental</option><option value="body-sensor">Body / opt-in health</option><option value="motion-sensor">Motion / orientation</option></select></label><button id="packet">Generate and validate synthetic sensor packet</button><pre id="packetout">No packet generated yet.</pre></div>
<p class="foot">Original architecture by Nathan Tabor. This is a reproducible research and software prototype, not a claim of self-awareness, immunity to corruption, comprehensive world sensing, a universal cure, or a physically operative void firewall.</p></main><script src="./engine.js"></script><script src="./mission-control.js"></script><script>
'use strict';const $=x=>document.getElementById(x);const E=TaborUniversalNode,M=TaborMissionControl;let state=E.make(73),latest=null;const escape=t=>String(t);
$('run').onclick=()=>{try{for(let i=0;i<20;i++)state=E.step(state,.1);$('rotation').textContent='Center (0, 0, 0) ECEF · X '+state.angles[0].toFixed(1)+'° · Y '+state.angles[1].toFixed(1)+'° · Z '+state.angles[2].toFixed(1)+'° · Cycle '+state.cycles}catch(e){$('rotation').textContent=e.message}};
$('example').onchange=()=>{const n=Number($('example').value);if($('example').value==='')return;const a=M.exampleCases()[n];$('domain').value=a.domain;$('risk').value=a.risk;$('evidence').value=a.evidenceStatus;$('title').value=a.title;$('description').value=a.description;$('severity').value=String(a.severity)};
$('assess').onclick=()=>{try{latest=M.assess({domain:$('domain').value,risk:$('risk').value,evidenceStatus:$('evidence').value,title:$('title').value,description:$('description').value,severity:Number($('severity').value),sources:$('source').value.trim()?[$('source').value.trim()]:[],consent:$('consent').checked,ownerApproval:$('approval').checked});$('mode').textContent=latest.mode+' · external action blocked';const out=$('gates');out.replaceChildren();for(const [key,g] of Object.entries(latest.gateChecks)){let d=document.createElement('div');d.className='box';let h=document.createElement('strong');h.textContent=g.name;let p=document.createElement('p');p.textContent=(g.passed?'Passed within the local checklist':'Needs review')+' — '+g.question;d.append(h,p);out.append(d)}const list=$('steps');list.replaceChildren();latest.steps.forEach(x=>{let li=document.createElement('li');li.textContent=x.name+(x.requiresApproval?' [approval required]':'');list.append(li)});$('advice').textContent=latest.advice}catch(e){$('mode').textContent='Input rejected: '+e.message}};
$('packet').onclick=()=>{try{const spec=M.deviceSpec($('device').value);const validation=M.validatePacket(spec.sample);$('packetout').textContent=JSON.stringify({spec,validation},null,2)}catch(e){$('packetout').textContent=e.message}};
$('export').onclick=()=>{if(!latest){$('mode').textContent='Run an analysis before exporting';return}const blob=new Blob([JSON.stringify(latest,null,2)],{type:'application/json'}),url=URL.createObjectURL(blob),a=document.createElement('a');a.href=url;a.download='tabor-universal-assessment.json';a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(url),1000)};
$('example').value='1';$('example').onchange();$('assess').click();</script></body></html>